# Slices 3/4 boundary: n - 1 = -1 does not fit size_t (row int -> size_t, receiver
# lm_stg_convert_int_size_t), so the edge of the composite argument refuses: that is `go`'s
# implicit throw `convert` (g = 3), as at a single value (unit_s3_arg_conv_range).  `take` is
# never called; uncaught, the root receives status 3, the entry has no value and the Message is
# stopped.  Mutant: the edge not emitted -- C converts -1 itself, `take` runs and the entry is 7.
fn: take (size_t: n) int
    return: 7
end: take
fn: go () int
    int: n 0
    return: take(n - 1)
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
